   "html_text": "To forgive is to respond in a particular way to someone who has treated someone badly or wrongly. In paradigmatic cases, forgiveness is a triadic relation between a wrong action φ, a wrongdoer and a wronged victim; the victim forgives the wrongdoer for having done φ. By forgiving, a victim can move on from φ while still judging that it was a culpable wrong. It has been claimed that the core of forgiveness is the giving up of certain negative emotions towards the wrongdoer, or the forbearance of ",
